      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The paper provides a socio-economic evaluation of mortality from ischemic heart disease (IHD) in Bulgaria during 1983-1985. The influence of IHD on mean life expectancy at birth was determined by using concise methods. IHD shortens the mean life expectancy in urban areas by 2.4 years in boys and by 1.7 years in girls, in rural areas by 2.5 years in boys and by 1.2 in girls. Economic losses due to mortality from this disease were estimated."},
